; ⚠️ 28px OF CLEARANCE AT THE TOP, NOT 8-12 — the same edge-band rule the bottom cards
; follow, applied to every HUD anchor rather than only the one that was reported. 🧑:
; *"do it for all huds, js raise it up all by a bit but not too much that it overlaps
; with something so that it doesnt keep on breaking bcz this is such a reoccuring
; issue"*. Asserted by `ui_layout_probe.gd` against TOP_SAFE_BAND; the bands and the
; reasoning for each number live there.
;
; ═══ TEAM CARD, LEFT ═══ Restyled 2026-07-30 to the menu's wood-and-amber language.
;
; Reported from play: the mid-game HUD "kinda doesnt look like our theme (menu and
; lobby), it looks ugly and plain and confusing". It was a near-white `card_style`
; panel — correct per the older §4.1 note, and nothing like the wood the front end
; actually shipped with.
;
; ⚠️ THE STYLEBOX IS NOT SET HERE. `hud.gd::_apply_wood_skin()` builds it from
; `UiTheme.wood_style()` — the same static call the menu's own `WoodSlot` uses — so the
; HUD cannot drift from the front end. It is done in code rather than as a theme
; variation only because the variations live in `ui_theme.gd`, which is ART's file and
; not writable by this lane; filed for ART to promote.
;
; ⚠️ THE LETTER MARK IS WHY THIS IS AN HBOX NOW. The hard rule is that team identity is
; the A/B letter and NEVER hue — but the letter was buried mid-string in "A · OFFENSE"
; at body size, so in practice hue was doing all the work and the two cards were
; distinguished only by which corner they sat in. The letter is now its own amber glyph
; at display size, and the ROLE word beside it carries the role colour.
;
; ⚠️ ZERO-WIDTH BOX ON PURPOSE — `offset_right == offset_left`. Reported on the first
; restyle render: *"big negative space in the ingame hud"*. The card was a fixed 250px
; and its content is a glyph plus a seven-letter word, so the right third was empty wood.
; A Control's size is clamped UP to its content minimum, which is the one place that rule
; is useful rather than a trap: a zero-width box hugs whatever is in it. TopRight does the
; same with `grow_horizontal = 0` so it grows leftward from the right anchor instead of
; off the screen.
;
; ⚠️ AND THAT IS WHY THE ROLE LABEL HAS NO `clip_text`. `clip_text` makes a Label report a
; zero minimum width — correct inside a fixed card, fatal inside a hugging one, where it
; would collapse the word to nothing. The two role strings are fixed constants of known
; length, so they are allowed to size the card. Anything variable-length must not go in
; here without giving the card a floor back.
; ═══ THE SCOREBOARD ═══
; ⚠️ THIS PANEL WAS `TopLeft`, A 2v2 TEAM CARD, AND EVERYTHING IN IT IS NEW.
; It held a big "A" letter mark, an OFFENSE/DEFENSE caption and a three-pip win row,
; and there was a `TopRight` mirroring it node-for-node for team B. Four players do not
; have teams and rounds are scored rather than won (`Design.md` §1, §8), so none of
; those five things describes anything that exists.
;
; `hud.gd` had been drawing the real scoreboard in CODE on top of them — hiding six
; nodes at `_build_scoreboard()` and appending four rows it built by hand — because the
; scene is this lane's file and `build core`'s pivot could not touch it. That was
; deliberate and it is § CHECKLIST 1.1. The four rows are AUTHORED HERE now; `hud.gd`
; binds them and fills them in.
[node name="Scoreboard" type="PanelContainer" parent="."]
