; R-27(b) — WHAT YOUR JOB IS THIS ROUND, on the one screen that had nothing to say.
; The ready phase told the player how to start the round and not what they were about
; to do in it. Sits ABOVE ReadyPrompt (which keeps the instruction) and is deliberately
; larger, because this is the headline and "press R" is the footnote.
;
; The colour is NOT set here — `hud.gd::show_ready_prompt()` tints the label OFFENSE or
; DEFENSE from the local unit's actual role, so it cannot disagree with the team cards
; along the top.
;
; ⚠️ NO PANEL BEHIND IT — TEXT ONLY, AND THAT IS THE SECOND ANSWER TO THIS PROBLEM.
; The legibility problem is real: bottom-centre of an FPP screen is where the viewmodel
; arms are, and role-blue on a full-brightness orange arm is the worst pairing on the
; screen. The first fix was a wood plate, and it was rejected on sight — *"it kinda looks
; ugly with that hud/ui, can u js do text there but stylized"*. Fair: two stacked boxes at
; the bottom of the frame fought the 3D instead of sitting on it.
;
; So legibility now comes from a heavy INK OUTLINE on the glyphs instead of a box behind
; them — set in `hud.gd::_apply_wood_skin()`, the same trick the screen-edge arrows use.
; It reads over the arms, over asphalt and over sky, and it adds no rectangle.
;
; CenterContainer so the label hugs its own text and stays centred at any aspect.
[node name="ReadyObjectiveRow" type="CenterContainer" parent="."]
